{
  "$comment": [
    "The release evidence gate's configuration, read at the release commit by scripts/dev/release_evidence.py",
    "(vendored from the development kit; its docs/ci-evidence.md is the contract, docs/releasing.md says how the",
    "release uses it). .github/test_ci_evidence.py holds this file to ci.yml and release.yml.",
    "Native sandbox coverage includes the Windows customer registration and approved-acquisition refusal."
  ],
  "schema": 2,
  "repository": "Judgment-Pack/judgment-pack-gateway",
  "branch": "main",
  "max_age_hours": 48,
  "inputs": [
    ".dockerignore",
    ".github/check_lanes.py",
    ".github/go_test_shard.py",
    ".github/workflows/release.yml",
    ".goreleaser.yml",
    "Dockerfile",
    "adapters/agreement/agreement_test.go",
    "adapters/gcpasset/testdata/resources-page.json",
    "adapters/gcpasset/testdata/resources-projected.json",
    "adapters/go.mod",
    "adapters/go.sum",
    "build/engine-image.sh",
    "build/mkhomes.go",
    "build/setcap.go",
    "catalog/postgres.json",
    "corpus/v3/stores/v3-descriptor-missing-snapshot.json",
    "corpus/v3/stores/v3-descriptor-missing-statement.json",
    "corpus/v3/stores/v3-descriptor-tampered-statement.json",
    "corpus/v3/stores/v3-descriptor-valid.json",
    "go/go.mod",
    "jpdev.json",
    "plugins/activepieces/judgment-pack/package-lock.json",
    "plugins/n8n-nodes-judgment-pack/package-lock.json",
    "scripts/checks/image-platforms.sh",
    "scripts/checks/image-root-unwritable.sh",
    "scripts/checks/witness-scenario.sh",
    "scripts/dev/changed_checks.py",
    "scripts/dev/check.sh",
    "testdata/attachments/schema-requirements.txt",
    "testdata/action-reconciliation/mutations.json",
    "testdata/descriptor-provenance/statement-mutations.json",
    "testdata/tool-descriptors/commonmark/go.mod",
    "testdata/tool-descriptors/commonmark/go.sum",
    "testdata/tool-descriptors/metaschema/go.mod",
    "testdata/tool-descriptors/metaschema/go.sum",
    "verify-ts/package-lock.json"
  ],
  "fresh_at_release": [
    "tag grammar, tag names the commit, commit on main",
    "release notes",
    "production environment reviewer",
    "third-party notices with the release toolchain",
    "packaging, packaged checksums, archive contents",
    "native archive runs: linux amd64 and arm64, macOS arm64, Windows amd64",
    "tag still names the commit, no release under the tag",
    "engine image built for linux amd64 and arm64, its index a release asset, each platform's filesystem held by image_checks.py",
    "attestation, of the archives and of the engine image",
    "draft identity",
    "production approval",
    "engine image pushed by digest and read back",
    "published asset digests"
  ],
  "profiles": {
    "check": {
      "$comment": [
        "The check job: the Go release.yml names, and Node and Python at the exact versions dev.json names.",
        "Held to its pins, not to the release runner: GitHub serves several builds of one runner image at once, so the image version is not ours to pin. Docker is the image's and the release job builds and checks the engine image itself, so it is not held here."
      ],
      "platform": {
        "RUNNER_OS": "Linux",
        "RUNNER_ARCH": "X64"
      },
      "compare": "pins",
      "tools": {
        "go": [
          "go",
          "version"
        ],
        "node": [
          "node",
          "--version"
        ],
        "python": [
          "python3",
          "--version"
        ]
      },
      "pins": {
        "go": "go version go1.26.5 linux/amd64",
        "node": "v22.23.4",
        "python": "Python 3.12.16"
      }
    },
    "go-linux": {
      "$comment": "The Linux leg of the go matrix: held to its pin, as the other legs are.",
      "platform": {
        "RUNNER_OS": "Linux",
        "RUNNER_ARCH": "X64"
      },
      "compare": "pins",
      "tools": {
        "go": [
          "go",
          "version"
        ]
      },
      "pins": {
        "go": "go version go1.26.5 linux/amd64"
      }
    },
    "go-macos": {
      "$comment": "The macOS leg: another OS and architecture than the release job's, so held to its pin.",
      "platform": {
        "RUNNER_OS": "macOS",
        "RUNNER_ARCH": "ARM64"
      },
      "compare": "pins",
      "tools": {
        "go": [
          "go",
          "version"
        ]
      },
      "pins": {
        "go": "go version go1.26.5 darwin/arm64"
      }
    },
    "go-windows": {
      "$comment": "The Windows leg: another OS than the release job's, so held to its pin.",
      "platform": {
        "RUNNER_OS": "Windows",
        "RUNNER_ARCH": "X64"
      },
      "compare": "pins",
      "tools": {
        "go": [
          "go",
          "version"
        ]
      },
      "pins": {
        "go": "go version go1.26.5 windows/amd64"
      }
    }
  },
  "workflows": {
    "ci": {
      "$comment": [
        "Only a push to main is evidence: ci.yml has no dispatch, so the fresh route is a re-run of all jobs of main's run.",
        "Every job and every matrix leg is required; none is skipped on main. The go legs include native adapter sandbox boundary tests (on Windows in the first shard) and run the workflow's own steps; the Windows leg runs the core's tests in two shards, each a leg of its own,",
        "not dev.json's, so their checks are none: the job's success is the API's, and the evidence adds the leg's",
        "platform and toolchain. The two check lanes run every dev.json check between them, each check in one lane, and each lane every setup step: a lane's evidence is its setup steps, the check job's every check's result, read from the lanes' summaries."
      ],
      "path": ".github/workflows/ci.yml",
      "name": "CI",
      "events": [
        "push"
      ],
      "jobs": {
        "check": {
          "name": "check",
          "job_id": "check",
          "labels": [
            "ubuntu-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "check",
          "checks": "all",
          "optional_skips": [],
          "setup": false
        },
        "check-go-tests": {
          "name": "check · go-tests",
          "job_id": "check-lanes",
          "labels": [
            "ubuntu-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "check",
          "checks": [],
          "setup": true
        },
        "check-rest": {
          "name": "check · rest",
          "job_id": "check-lanes",
          "labels": [
            "ubuntu-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "check",
          "checks": [],
          "setup": true
        },
        "go-ubuntu-latest": {
          "name": "ubuntu-latest · Go 1.26",
          "job_id": "go",
          "labels": [
            "ubuntu-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "go-linux",
          "checks": []
        },
        "go-macos-latest": {
          "name": "macos-latest · Go 1.26",
          "job_id": "go",
          "labels": [
            "macos-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "go-macos",
          "checks": []
        },
        "go-windows-latest-1": {
          "name": "windows-latest · Go 1.26 · shard 1 of 2",
          "job_id": "go",
          "labels": [
            "windows-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "go-windows",
          "checks": []
        },
        "go-windows-latest-2": {
          "name": "windows-latest · Go 1.26 · shard 2 of 2",
          "job_id": "go",
          "labels": [
            "windows-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "go-windows",
          "checks": []
        },
        "postgresql-superuser": {
          "name": "postgresql · superuser",
          "job_id": "postgresql",
          "labels": [
            "ubuntu-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "go-linux",
          "checks": []
        },
        "postgresql-non-superuser": {
          "name": "postgresql · non-superuser",
          "job_id": "postgresql",
          "labels": [
            "ubuntu-latest"
          ],
          "profile": "go-linux",
          "checks": []
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "tag": {
    "prerelease": true
  }
}
